rpp, wjvu a• lu
e3c1q
RESOLUTION NO.
5983
ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION PROVIDING FOR THE BUDGETING
OF
EXCESS 1% SPECIFIC PURPOSE SALES AND USE TAXES
COLLECTED FOR THE AUGUST 21, 2012 VOTER-APPROVED
SPECIFIC PURPOSES”
WHEREAS, at the primary election held on August 21, 2012 in Laramie County, the
voters approved specific purposes to be funded by the 1% specific purpose sales and use tax
(“voter-approved projects”); and
WHEREAS, pursuant to City Resolution 5374, Exhibit A, any excess tax funds, and
interest earned thereon (“excess tax funds”), shall be used for operation and maintenance of the
voter-approved projects or any other legal purpose with respect thereto; and
WHEREAS, Wyo. Stat. Ann. § 39-15-203(a)(iii)(B) prohibits revenues from the specific
purpose sales and use tax from being used to fund ordinary operations of local government; and
WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne, in preparation for Fiscal Year
2020, desires to budget for the operation and maintenance or capital construction expenses related
to the voter-approved projects;
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that:
1.
All excess tax funds are hereby appropriated for operation and maintenance or
capital construction expenses related to the August 21, 2012 voter-approved
projects; and
2.
City Staff is directed to prepare a priority list of any related or remaining capital
construction or operation and maintenance requests for the August 21, 2012 voter-
approved projects to be funded by the excess tax funds in Fiscal Year 2020 or
beyond. Items on the priority list will be considered by the Governing Body for
inclusion in the Fiscal Year 2020 Budget or City reserves.
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that this Resolution shall be effective upon passage and
execution by the Mayor and City Clerk.
PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this 25th
day of
March
,2019.
(Seal)
